      "message": "wouldn\u0027t it be better to define a constant that represents the MAX so you don\u0027t need to update so many sites in the code if a new attribute is enabled?\n\nDo this in the header file:\n```\nnum nl80211_tx_rate_attributes {\n\t__NL80211_TXRATE_INVALID,\n\tNL80211_TXRATE_LEGACY,\n\tNL80211_TXRATE_HT,\n\tNL80211_TXRATE_VHT,\n\tNL80211_TXRATE_GI,\n\tNL80211_TXRATE_HE,\n\tNL80211_TXRATE_HE_GI,\n\tNL80211_TXRATE_HE_LTF,\n\tNL80211_TXRATE_RESERVED_DO_NOT_USE_1,\n\tNL80211_TXRATE_RESERVED_DO_NOT_USE_2,\n\tNL80211_TXRATE_RESERVED_DO_NOT_USE_3,\n\tNL80211_TXRATE_RESERVED_DO_NOT_USE_4,\n\tNL80211_TXRATE_RESERVED_DO_NOT_USE_5,\n\t\n\t/* For new attributes */\n\t__NL80211_TXRATE_MAX_IMPLEMENTED \u003d NL80211_TXRATE_HE_LTF,\n\n\t/* keep last */\n\t__NL80211_TXRATE_AFTER_LAST,\n\tNL80211_TXRATE_MAX \u003d __NL80211_TXRATE_AFTER_LAST - 1\n};\n```\n\nThen you\u0027d use `__NL80211_TXRATE_MAX_IMPLEMENTED + 1` to size the array",
